    "updated_at": "2019-10-16T07:49:57Z",
    "body": "From a primitives perspective, either way we need to define in HTML that elements have some kind of \"focus visible\" flag, that's to be set per platform / user agent conventions. And then we define that `:focus-visible` matches elements that have that flag set.\r\n\r\nGiven that needs to be there anway, the former of your two options does not seem that complex to me and avoids developers having to duplicate styles and be aware there's two states (`:focus-visible` and a custom class) for what is essentially a single state.",
